# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Build output. The icons under build/ are generated by tools/genicons.py and
# committed, so a clone needs neither Python nor Pillow to build; the binaries
# beside them are not.
build/bin/
frontend/dist/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/package.json.md5
installer/build/bin/
installer/frontend/wailsjs/
dist-installer/

# installer/payload.zip is deliberately NOT ignored: it is committed as an
# empty-zip placeholder so `go build ./...` works in a fresh clone. build.ps1
# stages the real payload into it and puts the placeholder back afterwards, so
# a payload of megabytes never reaches a commit.

# Wails writes its generated bindings here. They are not the wire contract:
# frontend/src/api.ts is, and tests/structural/wire_test.go compares it with
# the Go DTOs.
frontend/wailsjs/

# Local scratch notes.
NOTES.md
resume.md
.claude/resume.md
